//! SSH connections (System → SSH): servers the hub reaches with keys it holds, attached to
//! projects and groups with a note on what they are for there.
//!
//! - A key is generated by the hub (ed25519, `ssh-keygen`) or imported; the private key is
//!   encrypted like project secrets and never returned. People copy the public key into the
//!   server's `authorized_keys`.
//! - "Test" connects once and pins the server's host keys; later connections refuse a
//!   changed host key.
//! - An agent session of a project or group gets its connections without seeing a key:
//!   the hub starts an ssh-agent for the turn with those keys, writes an ssh config with an
//!   alias per connection and wrappers for `ssh` / `scp` / `sftp` (and `GIT_SSH_COMMAND`),
//!   bind-mounts that folder into the sandbox, and lists the connections with their
//!   descriptions in the agent's context — the description tells the agent prod from dev.
//!
//! A private key in the clear exists only in memory, in the ssh-agent, and for a moment in a
//! private folder under the runtime dir (tmpfs: `ssh-keygen` and `ssh -i` want a file). The
//! per-turn agents are stopped with the turn, on hub exit (`dispose_all`), and — after a
//! crash — by the sweep on the next start (`sweep_runtime`).
//!
//! A port of `ssh.ts`; both servers run the same `ssh-keygen` / `ssh` commands.

